-- title:
--   Unipotent flat model for the twisted dual ̄ V^∨(1)
-- statement:
--   Fix a finite field $k$ of characteristic $p$ with $p$ prime and $p \neq 2$, together with a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra structure on $\mathbb{Z}/p$ whose structure map has kernel the ideal generated by $p$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual representation over $k$, i.e. a two-dimensional $k$-space $V$ with a homomorphism $\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to $\mathrm{End}_k V$ that is trivial on the elements fixing some finite subextension $L/\mathbb{Q}$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Assume (hypothesis `hconn`) that there is a commutative ring $H$ carrying a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-Hopf algebra structure, finite and flat as a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-module and cocommutative, such that $\mathbb{Z}/p \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} H$ is a local ring, and a bijection $e$ from the convolution group $\mathrm{Hom}_{\mathbb{Z}_p\text{-alg}}(H, \overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p)$ onto $V \times V$ carrying the product to addition and intertwining the action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p/\mathbb{Q}_p)$ on points (post-composition with $\sigma$) with the diagonal action $x \mapsto (\rho(\sigma^{\mathrm{glob}})x_1, \rho(\sigma^{\mathrm{glob}})x_2)$, this being `dualLiftModuleActAd` at the zero cocycle and $\sigma^{\mathrm{glob}}$ the image of $\sigma$ under `primeLocalToGlobal`. Let further $\bar\rho'$ be a residual representation over $k$ and $\eta : V' \xrightarrow{\sim} \mathrm{Hom}_k(V,k)$ a $k$-linear isomorphism with $\eta(\rho'(g)w) = \bar\chi(g)\,(\eta(w) \circ \rho(g^{-1}))$ for all global $g$ and all $w$, where $\bar\chi(g)$ is the image in $k$ of the mod-$p$ cyclotomic character `cycloChar`; thus $\bar\rho' \cong \bar\rho^\vee(1)$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a commutative ring $H'$ with a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-Hopf algebra structure, finite and flat over $\mathbb{Z}_p$ and cocommutative, such that the Cartier dual $\mathrm{Hom}_{\mathbb{Z}/p}(\mathbb{Z}/p \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} H', \mathbb{Z}/p)$ is a local ring, together with a bijection from $\mathrm{Hom}_{\mathbb{Z}_p\text{-alg}}(H', \overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p)$ onto $V' \times V'$ turning the convolution product into addition and equivariant for the local Galois action on points against the same diagonal action $\bar\rho' \oplus \bar\rho'$.
--
--   This is the Cartier-duality step in the study of models at $p$: a finite flat model of $\bar V \oplus \bar V$ with connected special fibre dualises to a finite flat model of $\bar V^\vee(1) \oplus \bar V^\vee(1)$ whose special fibre is unipotent, expressed here as the locality of the Cartier dual of the special fibre. It is used by [`ResidualGaloisRep.exists_unipotent_model_and_linearEquiv_localFlatClassesAd_of_isLocalRing_baseChange`](thm.html#ResidualGaloisRep.exists_unipotent_model_and_linearEquiv_localFlatClassesAd_of_isLocalRing_baseChange) in the treatment of the flat local condition at $p$.
